### RQL String Functions

- Published: 2014-12-16
- Modified: 2021-07-16
- URL: https://rollbar.com/blog/rql-string-functions/
- Categories: product
- Tags: triage

RQL now includes a basic library of string functions. You can use these to slice and group your data in arbitrary ways. For example, "email domains with the most events in the past hour": SELECT substring(person. email, locate('@', person. email)), count(*) FROM item_occurrence WHERE timestamp >= unix_timestamp - 3600 AND person. email IS NOT NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC The new functions: concat, concat_ws, lower, upper, left, right, substring, locate, length, char_length. The functions are implemented to be compatible with MySQL; see the RQL docs for details.

