We've released a new version of our Node. js library, version 0. 3. 11. It's available on npm and GitHub. This release adds a new function to the public API, handleErrorWithPayloadData. The name's a mouthful, but it allows you to use (nearly) the full power of the Rollbar API when reporting errors. For example, to report an error as a "warning" and pass some additional data: rollbar. handleErrorWithPayloadData(err, {level: "warning", custom: {someKey: "some value"}}); See more examples in the docs for caught exceptions.

